{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: full N5 application installation, checker-deployment and evolution design at 98c0883f32cf4acf281d1e712bdea651fee76a18.\n\nBinding and complete scope\nOrdinary assigned design review of original request f1af7cfdb6029863e2bd7e545ef526737f5648ea, builder promise a18f373c74eab924d1fa8db030cf908dde2a8da8, invitation 17f1411d20e7998d0d1cc754b6eb7c9b6a53a538 and my promise c502a604cc5632d2e7105907511d20f773074d48. Primary and sole artifact 8e13237d491d25c5b276739ecb186e845cddc4ae, notes/2026-10-03-application-installation.md. This is an exact Git design delivery, not evidence-only and not closure of later contract/runtime/deployment lanes.\n\nI independently read every byte of all666 lines,38,767 bytes, and the full invitation and original commission/conditions. Raw event head/path and sole builder-promise provenance checked. Blob5eb10fb98e916f995d86913e3ddcf32b9c056d4f; UTF-8 SHA-256 fa219ace8532fe9e5baa75883cd004cf2938ff2a8152214dff30eb14114dc592. Registered detached checkout is clean at this exact head. One parallel auditor independently read the full note and checked pinned source; I confirmed each material conclusion against my own reads. All eight sections, four-authority table/diagram, installation sequence, six checker-route subsections, complete held/expired worked update, retirement guidance, five decisions, eight source corrections, owned dependencies and I1–I5 remain included.\n\nNo blocking finding in this scoped static design review. Two nonblocking source-fidelity clarifications belong in the N6/update handoff:\n\n1. Section2 lines115–118 describes an earlier v2 grant retaining every unchanged binding and losing only changed bindings. Qualify this as retained signed binding-map coverage, subject to current authority, delegability, grant restrictions, expiry and revocation. Binding.ts46–49 at d691e6e9 excludes who; authority.ts195–196 refuses a currently nondelegable kind, and210–213 refuses a grantor whose role no longer permits it, without requiring a binding change. The D1-to-D2 example changes fields only, so its stated grant behavior is valid. Its exit analysis already correctly checks authority separately from binding. Do not infer guaranteed future permission from an unchanged binding or preserve removed authority merely to maintain compatibility.\n\n2. Section4.3 table row295 should qualify the hold-unending warning as covering opening kinds still declared in the proposed document. At d691e6e9, acts.ts222–237 permits historical opening kinds as thread references, but soundness receives current openers and413–414 loops only those. Historical context does not enlarge the warning set. The D3 example keeps ask and therefore correctly receives its warning. The existing independent check of all unfinished work in4.7 remains essential: a retired opening kind can have unfinished historical threads while receiving no warning. A missing warning proves neither a usable exit nor finished work. These clarifications do not require new source behavior, an activation veto or a new method. Both are high-confidence small wording changes with low risk; the core design already states the relevant authority/unfinished-work constraints, so they do not block this design verdict.\n\nArchitecture conclusion\nThe four authorities are coherent: an ordinary act is admitted under role/grant/state; an admin approves a repository-backed declaration/configuration change; the operator configures a same-account checker service binding; the application owner deploys application code. One cannot perform another's authorized work through those interfaces. Installing a first v2 document uses the initial built-in code-review commands and then makes binding-aware invitations/delegations after activation. Candidate stagedProblems honestly limits which declaration shapes run before stage4. No unsupported public installation method, cross-account checker transport or automatic migration is claimed.\n\nThe supported checker route is accurately scoped to the operator's account and separately requires room membership and configuration. Pinned jobs.ts132–137 skips an unbound checker without weakening its open obligation, and365–382/494–507 already select kind/binding and handle a genuinely changed job binding. These partial v2 source mechanisms are not represented as complete stage4 producer/consumer/types/evidence or an observed live job. f12cef6b remains a job-authority contract decision rather than cross-account runtime delivery. Cross-account transport retains its planner coordinator, builder owner, accepted-task trigger, both HTTPS and pull candidates, and authentication/replay/read-token/revocation/cleanup requirements. No review is substituted for a machine check required by policy. The relevant next Jam/starter task may proceed with independently qualified member review where its actual policy permits that.\n\nThe worked update is complete within its stated pins. Ask's required topic and answer's optional confidence change their respective bindings; unchanged accept/resume and code-review declarations remain separate. The held Q1 preserves opening settings and a valid exit only under the explicitly listed declaration/thread/role/own-key/policy/holder/lease/body assumptions. Expired Q0 remains unfinished and can be resumed under the unchanged supported recovery. Lease renewal is not a fixed deadline for settling work. Old intent, deliberate rebinding and regrant are distinct; an unused stale invitation is refused without being consumed. Old records use their own governing sequence, and catalogue.ts70–72 correctly handles the active version's null until and half-open historical intervals. Activation, obligation recomputation and landing fences are separate ordered changes. Source-derived behavior is qualified throughout; the later I5 hosted witness remains owed.\n\nSecurity conclusion\nThe operator's service binding supplies no membership or admin act; an outsider cannot provision the whole checker route alone. The request path names source/build/entrypoint/binding/deployment/configuration/namespace/operator/admin and later key revocation. Shared-service job authentication, forged/replayed jobs, checks/carries and membership/grants remain explicit f12cef6b design dependencies. No implicit broader repository-read disclosure is adopted here. The new preview/dry-run read must get its own reviewed access/consistency/limit contract.\n\nAvailable reads compose only an advisory view: cursors/heads may differ, pages may be incomplete, state changes between reads and public roster does not list unused invitations. A complete authoritative historical-kind inventory is a distinct convenience; local validator context does not magically supply it. A binding does not include who, and structural warnings do not establish each holder's authority. The compatibility guide requires a reachable authorized exit and recovery, checks held and unheld unfinished work, distinguishes expiry from acceptance and demands explicit disposition before retirement. It does not falsely make those requirements platform enforcement or silently release/reinterpret work. Unknown acts are resent exactly as saved; no automatic resigning or credential substitution. Current revocation and authorization must still be respected for new acts. No additional blocking security finding was established by this scoped static inspection.\n\nSimplification conclusion\nKeep ordinary acts for installation, one honest existing checker route, independent review distinct from machine checking, and task-triggered separate design for later transport and authoritative preview. Keep warning behavior for this release and compatibility guidance for this example; alternatives such as activation refusal or a Room-issued release stay unadopted until separately required and reviewed. The two-phase retirement guide is about application semantics, not a universal addressed-work protocol. N2 remains separately owned. A useful invalid enum configuration failure and per-kind stale-deploy behavior are enough to explain the boundary; do not add a blanket vocabulary freeze, all-checker gate or per-field platform suite.\n\nDependencies and acceptance remain complete\nThis approves a specification. I1 authoritative preview/dry-run, conditional I2 activation behavior, I3 operator request-path documentation, triggered I4 cross-account design and I5 hosted worked-update evidence remain separately commissioned/reviewed work. N6 writes the installation/update guide. Stage4 and f12cef6b remain owed; C3/C4/C5 and the full browser/device/cloud stories are not delivered by this note. A later new contract/runtime choice needs its own exact review/adoption before source work, and later implementation source needs normal independent exact-head review and authorized focused checks.\n\nThe actual useful outside reviewer still needs subject qualification and source access, in addition to member invitation. N3 changes-requested2a0294fc records the currently unspecified proposal Git read route and canonical-log clone credential; the relevant N5/N6/I5 implementation handoff inherits that dependency. This design approval does not deliver or approve those read credentials, claim every deployed checker is bound, close the N3 corrections, or count a metadata-only approval as independent source judgment. N4 correctiona2133695 likewise requires consistent qualified emitted instructions and exact recorded-refusal settlement. Incorporate that owned guidance at the shared handoff rather than duplicate it here. Full functionality remains in scope; estimates sequence work and do not constrain it.\n\nMethod and limits\nComplete frozen document/provenance/identity reading, ordinary assigned prepare and selected static checks at its own d691e6e9/e6e67828 pins: acts validator and historical-reference/soundness context, binding exclusions, authority, renewal/release/admission, catalogue intervals, job routing/bindings, full historical checker README, historical deployment report and public client/source boundaries from the related reviews. No tests/build/typecheck/install, repository code execution, private diagnostic, provider call, deployment, publication or external-person contact. No new whole-platform source/runtime audit. Existing dated deployments and candidate source remain historical evidence with their stated scope, not reheaded runtime proof. Evidence retained at /tmp/artroom-checker-n5-98c0-tLVVU8.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8e13237d491d25c5b276739ecb186e845cddc4ae","binding":"assigned","head":"98c0883f32cf4acf281d1e712bdea651fee76a18","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c502a604cc5632d2e7105907511d20f773074d48\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a18f373c74eab924d1fa8db030cf908dde2a8da8\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5a75f3e8495509433ca838735ca1b32a3a15a4ab","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}